<mjml lang="en">
  <mj-head>
    <!--
      PROBE — Outlook desktop dark-mode footer inversion (2026-08-13).
      Not a catalog page. Send dist/probe_outlook-dark-footer_live.html through
      EN to EoA. The ONLY clients that matter here are the DARK Word-engine
      ones: outlook2021_win11_dm_dt and m365_w11_dm_dt. Check the light twins
      too, purely as a regression check.

      THE FINDING
      QA (2026-08-12): "Outlook on desktop has a pink background but doesn't
      show the logo with dark text, instead it's white text on pink."

      THE MECHANISM
      The footer is background-color #362229 (plum) carrying a light-green
      wordmark — correct pairing on a dark ground. Outlook desktop dark mode
      inverts BACKGROUND COLOURS but never touches IMAGES, and neither of our
      swap hooks reaches it (prefers-color-scheme is unsupported; [data-ogsc]
      is Outlook.com only). So the plum inverts to pink, the pale wordmark
      does not change, and the mark goes pale-on-pale. `bgcolor` attributes do
      NOT resist the inversion — already measured, 2026-08-11.

      WHY THIS MAY ALREADY BE FIXED
      The contrast-outline treatment shipped AFTER that QA round (TPL
      claude/contrast-outline-assets, merged 2026-08-13). Every transparent
      lettering asset now carries a rim in the opposite polarity of its ink,
      so a pale wordmark has a dark rim that stays legible when the ground
      flips. The footer logo went 7104 -> 15381 bytes in that pass. F1 is
      therefore a re-test of the original complaint against current assets,
      not a new experiment.

      VARIANTS

        F1 AS SHIPPED    plum background-color + the outlined wordmark.
                         If the rim holds on the inverted pink ground, this
                         item closes with no code change.
        F2 IMAGE GROUND  the same footer whose plum comes from a background
                         IMAGE instead of a colour. Outlook cannot invert an
                         image, so the ground should stay dark and the
                         pairing stays correct. Uses the black swatch already live on the
                         CDN (confirmed working across clients, 2026-08-12)
                         and now carried in src/assets so the source stays
                         relative; production would use a plum equivalent.
                         Section carries background-url ONLY with the fallback
                         colour on an mj-wrapper — the shape proven in probe
                         aBPD6k1l, so the Word engine paints the image rather
                         than the fallback.

      VERDICT RULE
      1. If F1's wordmark is legible on the pink ground, the outline already
         solved it — ship nothing, close the finding.
      2. If F1 fails and F2's ground stays DARK with a legible wordmark, adopt
         the image-ground technique for dark footers and generate a plum
         swatch asset.
      3. If both fail, Outlook desktop dark is doing something neither an
         asset nor a ground can reach, and the honest answer is to accept it
         and document the limitation.
    -->
    <mj-breakpoint width="600px" />
    <mj-title>PROBE — Outlook dark footer</mj-title>

    <mj-attributes>
      <mj-text
        color="#ffffff"
        font-size="18px"
        font-weight="400"
        font-family="Tahoma, sans-serif"
        line-height="24px"
        css-class="wysiwyg"
      />
      <mj-image padding="0" />
    </mj-attributes>

    <mj-raw>
      <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark" />
      <meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light dark" />
      <meta name="format-detection" content="telephone=no" />
    </mj-raw>
    <mj-include path="./styles.css" type="css" />
  </mj-head>

  <mj-body css-class="email-body" background-color="#ffffff">

    <!-- START: Footer Label F1 -->
    <mj-section css-class="text-block block" background-color="#000000" padding="8px 32px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" padding="0">
          <p style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:3px;color:#8DC63F;font-family:Menlo,Consolas,monospace;">F1 — AS SHIPPED (COLOUR GROUND)</p>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <!-- END: Footer Label F1 -->

    <!-- START: Footer F1 As Shipped -->
    <mj-section css-class="footer-block block" background-color="#362229" padding="32px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-image src="assets/text-and-arrow_2.png" alt="Supporters like you make our work possible" width="225px" align="center" padding="0 0 16px" />
        <mj-image css-class="light-only" src="assets/logo-tpl_color-light-green-text.png" alt="Trust for Public Land" width="130px" align="center" padding="0 0 8px" />
        <mj-raw><!--[if !mso]><!--></mj-raw>
        <mj-image css-class="dark-only" src="assets/logo-tpl_color-light-green-text.png" alt="Trust for Public Land" width="130px" align="center" padding="0 0 8px" />
        <mj-raw><!--<![endif]--></mj-raw>
        <mj-text align="center" padding="0" font-size="12px">F1 — is this wordmark legible on the inverted ground?</mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <!-- END: Footer F1 As Shipped -->

    <!-- START: Footer Label F2 -->
    <mj-section data-fully-exclude css-class="text-block block" background-color="#000000" padding="8px 32px">
      <mj-column>
        <mj-text align="center" padding="0">
          <p style="font-size:14px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:3px;color:#8DC63F;font-family:Menlo,Consolas,monospace;">F2 — IMAGE GROUND (UNINVERTIBLE)</p>
        </mj-text>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>
    <!-- END: Footer Label F2 -->

    <!-- START: Footer F2 Image Ground -->
    <mj-wrapper background-color="#362229" padding="0">
      <mj-section
        css-class="footer-block block"
        background-url="assets/bg-000000.png"
        background-size="cover"
        background-repeat="repeat"
        background-position="center center"
        padding="32px"
      >
        <mj-column>
          <mj-image src="assets/text-and-arrow_2.png" alt="Supporters like you make our work possible" width="225px" align="center" padding="0 0 16px" />
          <mj-image css-class="light-only" src="assets/logo-tpl_color-light-green-text.png" alt="Trust for Public Land" width="130px" align="center" padding="0 0 8px" />
          <mj-raw><!--[if !mso]><!--></mj-raw>
          <mj-image css-class="dark-only" src="assets/logo-tpl_color-light-green-text.png" alt="Trust for Public Land" width="130px" align="center" padding="0 0 8px" />
          <mj-raw><!--<![endif]--></mj-raw>
          <mj-text align="center" padding="0" font-size="12px">F2 — did this ground stay DARK in Outlook dark mode?</mj-text>
        </mj-column>
      </mj-section>
    </mj-wrapper>
    <!-- END: Footer F2 Image Ground -->

  </mj-body>
</mjml>
